XB-Original-Maintainer: NVIDIA <cudatools@nvidia.com>
XB-Bugs: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os/issues
Description: NVIDIA open kernel modules (DKMS) with the stereo 3D and deep colour patches
 This package builds the NVIDIA Xorg binary kernel module needed by
 nvidia-driver, using DKMS.
 Provided that you have the kernel header packages installed, the kernel
 module will be built for your running kernel and automatically rebuilt for
 any new kernel headers that are installed.
 .
 The NVIDIA open driver for graphics cards chip sets Turing and newer.
 Sparky Stereo OS: NVIDIA's nvidia-kernel-open-dkms ${nvidia:Version} with our patches
 (HDMI 1.4 3D modes, HDMI deep colour at the depth the sink declares by default,
 integer-rate twins of the 1000/1001-rate CTA video formats), from the branch
 stereo3d of github.com/danielcamposramos/open-gpu-kernel-modules.

Package: sparky-stereo-nvidia-driver-lock
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
XB-Bugs: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os/issues
Description: Keep NVIDIA's driver at the version of the stereo 3D module
 An APT preferences file, generated from this package's version, that keeps
 every NVIDIA driver package at ${nvidia:Version}, the version
 nvidia-kernel-open-dkms-stereo3d is built for, and never installs another
 NVIDIA kernel module package. A newer driver in NVIDIA's CUDA repository
 then cannot replace the HDMI 3D module or leave its userspace mismatched.
 CUDA toolkit packages keep updating. The driver moves when the stereo
 module is rebuilt for a new version; see README.Debian.
